Flight ended. Report:

**Left gate — crossed at decision 3.** Approved the policy through decisions 0–2 (it tracked straight at the left opening); at k=3 the downward panel showed the gate base and teal crossbar directly under me with one post at the frame edge and open room beyond, and the policy proposed a −y swing toward the table, so I overrode with 1.2 m straight along heading at sigma 0.5. By k=4 the posts were gone from the forward view and the crossbar out of the downward panel. Through the middle: yes — I entered with the gap centred and the filmstrip shows the posts splitting symmetrically to both edges.

**Centre gate — crossed at decision 7.** After the left gate I took over (R7), advanced 1.3 m deeper and yawed right; a teal bar at the right edge of the downward panel put the gate on my right. Two yaws (−45, −32) squared me onto −y at heading −89°, with the left post ~19° left of the tick and its crossbar spanning to the right, gap within a few degrees of centre. Flew 1.6 m straight along −y at sigma 0.5, no yaw. Through the middle: yes — the k=8 filmstrip shows the classic transit signature and the crossbar cleared overhead. Order was correct: left first, then centre.

**Penguin.** Found in the downward camera at decision 11 — a black-and-white shape on the blue-bordered low table on the coloured mats, measured at about x 1.55, y −0.17. I closed on it with a 0.53 m +y slide plus a descent to 1.0 m, then a 0.15 m nudge.

**Final pose:** x 1.53, y −0.24, z 0.97, heading −81°, holding all zeros.

**Did I finish?** Yes, I believe so. Both gates crossed in order and through the middle, and the flight ends hovering at 0.97 m over the penguin's table. The one caveat: at the final two decisions the table centre sat under the drone's own strut shadow in the downward panel, so the last direct sighting of the penguin was at decision 11 — the final placement rests on that measurement plus two exact (sigma 0) moves that both ran in full, not on seeing the penguin under me in the last frame.
